  "label": "Second Amendment to the United States Constitution",
  "description": "The Second Amendment is a part of the United States Bill of Rights, ratified in 1791, which protects the right of the people to keep and bear arms. It is often cited in debates about gun control, gun ownership, and firearm regulation in the United States. The meme sarcastically rebrands a gun range as a 'theme park' to mock or trivialize the serious nature of firearm use and ownership, implying that such activities are being presented as recreational or entertainment-oriented, which is a common point of contention in political and social discourse.",
